=== Baptisms
--- Baptism in Romans 6 [title]
overline: Romans 6 • Baptisms
heading: Baptism in Romans 6
sub: “Baptized into Christ” • Spiritual Union vs. Water Baptism

--- Baptized into Christ
kicker: Baptism in Romans 6
p: The Greek word **baptisma** means to immerse or become part of by immersion. In the New Testament it does **not always** refer to water baptism. In Romans 6, Paul describes believers being **baptized into Jesus Christ** and **into his death** (vv. 3-4)—a **spiritual reality** accomplished by the Holy Spirit at the moment of faith, placing us in union with Christ's death, burial, and resurrection. This is the **baptism of regeneration** (the baptism with fire). It is **not** referring to water baptism, which is only an outward symbol.

--- Spiritual Baptism and Water Baptism (1)
kicker: Baptism in Romans 6
table: Spiritual Baptism into Christ | Water Baptism
tr: **By the Holy Spirit • Real Union • Regeneration** | **Outward Symbol • Ordinance • Testimony**
tr: [[Romans 6:3-4]] | An outward act in water, picturing the spiritual reality already accomplished.
tr: [[1 Corinthians 12:13]] | Performed by men (e.g., Philip baptizing the eunuch in water – [[Acts 8:36-38]]).
tr: [[Galatians 3:27]] | Follows faith; a public testimony ([[Acts 8:36-38]]).

--- Spiritual Baptism and Water Baptism (2)
kicker: Baptism in Romans 6
table: Spiritual Baptism into Christ | Water Baptism
tr: Places believer **in Christ** instantly upon faith; the real identification that makes us dead to sin and alive to God. | A **like figure** (symbol) of salvation, not the cause ([[1 Peter 3:21]]).
tr: Happens to **all true believers** the moment they believe; no delay possible. | Can be separated from receiving the Spirit ([[Acts 8:12-16]] – Samaritans baptized in water but later received the Spirit; [[Acts 10:44-48]] – Cornelius’ household received Spirit first, then water baptized).

--- Spiritual Baptism and Water Baptism (3)
kicker: Baptism in Romans 6
table: Spiritual Baptism into Christ | Water Baptism
tr: The **baptism with the Holy Ghost and fire** that John said Christ would bring ([[Matthew 3:11|Matt. 3:11]]); regeneration itself. | John preached “the baptism of repentance” (change of mind) to prepare for Christ ([[Mark 1:4]]; [[Acts 19:4]]).
tr: Paul’s primary mission: the spiritual baptism that unites us to Christ ([[1 Corinthians 1:17|1 Cor. 1:17]] – Christ sent me not to baptize [in water], but to preach the gospel). | Important ordinance, but secondary to the gospel; Paul distinguished it from his main calling.

--- Key Insight
kicker: Baptism in Romans 6
callout: Key Insight: Water baptism and the Spirit’s baptism are sometimes separate in Acts, proving they are **distinct**. The baptism in Romans 6 is the **spiritual placement into Christ**—the real union that makes us dead to sin and alive to God through the baptism of regeneration by the Holy Spirit.

